<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-09-28T16:50:02Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>For a 'measured diplomatic figure', Pope Leo's visit to France has been 'deeply political'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e8e33b80422912ff5edeadcfc70c6ec5512058bca4df698559ec6470799f5094</id><updated>2026-09-28T16:50:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T15:46:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/for-a-measured-diplomatic-figure-pope-leo-s-visit-to-france-has-been-deeply-political" /><summary type="html">Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Colleen Dulle, Vatican correspondent for America magazine and author of "Struck Down, Not Destroyed". She came to Pope Leo’s visit to France expecting measured diplomacy but was struck by how deeply political the trip became. She observed a pope trying to articulate a vision of Europe shaped simultaneously by its Christian inheritance, its history of conflict, its encounter with other cultures, and its responsibility to pursue peace. His choice of Metz itself was significant. For Leo, this is a place where historic enemies transformed their relationship through reconciliation and cooperation, making Europe itself part of his message.</summary></entry><entry><title>Hybrid warfare: The threat of Russia looms over the Mediterranean</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:28a18edd4e08e42afccf0a7aa455676d414c2b4abee1a92e890413484d3d03c5</id><updated>2026-09-28T16:50:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T15:39:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260928-hybrid-warfare-the-threat-of-russia-looms-over-the-mediterranean" /><summary type="html">The CIA has reportedly warned several countries that Russia is preparing to launch hybrid operations across the Mediterranean Sea. But is the risk real, or is it a form of cyber warfare?</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>🔴 Five men arrested over suspected bomb plot at UK air base to be released on bail</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:65e044af0632464846085a2779841d3f1a9aba8e094cfab81c8e2c8d72482038</id><updated>2026-09-28T16:50:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T15:05:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260928-five-men-arrested-suspected-bomb-plot-uk-air-base-to-be-released-on-bail-fairford" /></entry><entry><title>UK police bail five men held over suspected bomb plot at US-run air base</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3b159ae50865cec7ec5826622f98bc5371e20cf6cd2cc7e09fe99cff104b1a24</id><updated>2026-09-28T16:50:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T15:01:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260928-five-men-arrested-suspected-bomb-plot-uk-air-base-to-be-released-on-bail-fairford" /><summary type="html">British police said Monday that five men arrested on explosives and terror charges near a US-run air base in England were being released on bail but remained under investigation. Counter-terror detectives said they were investigating "multiple lines of inquiry", including whether there is a link to Iran.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>French far right's Jordan Bardella denies alleged 2013 anti-Semitic comments</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:be60cc842fab72f338e67511989b97270699d9e17518c82fbde4c4d138beb7f8</id><updated>2026-09-28T16:50:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T14:45:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260928-french-far-right-jordan-bardella-denies-alleged-2013-anti-semitic-comments-mediapart-lepen" /><summary type="html">Jordan Bardella, the head of Marine Le Pen's National Rally (RN) party, has denied allegations made by French investigative website Mediapart that he wrote anti-Semitic comments on private chats in 2013, when he was aged 17 or 18. Bardella, seen as a likely prime minister if Le Pen wins next year's presidential election, said he would take legal action over the claims.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>'Fascinating success': Pope Leo’s appeal in France transcends faith and politics</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6adf2f6ac6593b3143ffa88967bccafdaf094a65861af470c5bf015389cb9996</id><updated>2026-09-28T16:50:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T14:35:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/fascinating-success-pope-leo-s-appeal-in-france-transcends-faith-and-politics" /><summary type="html">Annette Young is pleased to welcome Victor GAETAN, Senior International Correspondent for the National Catholic Register. He sees Pope Leo XIV's visit to France as more than a successful pastoral journey. He says it offers a window into the intellectual and political character of Leo's nascent papacy. What has been particularly striking is the breadth of his appeal: Leo has been welcomed by people of different faiths and across France's political spectrum. He also sees a direct intellectual connection between the present Pope and Leo XIII, particularly through Rerum Novarum, which confronted the social consequences of technological and economic transformation at the end of the XIX century.</summary></entry><entry><title>A Green pope? Vatican describes environmental destruction as an 'ecological sin'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9bf0284db61cc3a942fdef178da854693c2242a563b6611dd7b505d257e09c22</id><updated>2026-09-28T16:50:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T14:19:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/down-to-earth/20260928-a-green-pope-vatican-describes-environmental-destruction-as-an-ecological-sin" /><summary type="html">In recent years, the Catholic Church has taken a growing stance in favour of climate action, culminating with the Vatican's signing of the landmark Paris climate agreement in 2022. As Pope Leo wraps up his four-day visit to France, FRANCE 24's Valerie Dekimpe looks at where religion and the environment meet.</summary><category term="Down to Earth" /></entry><entry><title>French Senate elections: What next after far right surge?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:602c6c7e8b06437001455ff40d8df9ed1311218e4985d56f9eab5e9c8c93e477</id><updated>2026-09-28T16:50:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T14:14:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260928-french-senate-elections-what-next-after-far-right-surge" /><summary type="html">The far-right party of Marine Le Pen will for the first time in its history be able to form a parliamentary group in the French upper house, election results showed Monday, a political breakthrough just over half a year before presidential polls. France 24's Marc Perelman takes a look at how much of a boost the result might be to Le Pen's National Rally.</summary></entry><entry><title>🔴 Live: Pope Leo leads Mass at Metz Cathedral on final leg of visit to France</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1a4aac63cec3cf128a9bff5d3f69760773f88baae325b072a9bbe1389bfd6dce</id><updated>2026-09-28T16:50:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T14:14:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260928-live-pope-leo-xiv-arrives-in-metz-for-final-stop-of-france-visit" /></entry><entry><title>Heavy rain and flooding kills dozens northern India</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f4cb30ed90025fc36fce92cdb22984203237ad07a6fa5ed81c3b372ac48f16ea</id><updated>2026-09-28T16:50:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T14:03:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260928-heavy-rain-and-flooding-kills-dozens-northern-india" /><summary type="html">The death toll from floods triggered by heavy rain in the northern Indian state of Uttar Pradesh rose to 81, the government's disaster agency said. Uttar Pradesh, India's most populous state with more than 240 million people, is frequently lashed by rain and thunderstorms during the monsoon rainy season from June to September.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump heads to GOP strongholds Alabama and Oklahoma to campaign for midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e99b26f50fe4604ac2fe95eee8cabdcfa0269b2c24cb5530604b46c5860e8363</id><updated>2026-09-28T16:50:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T13:59:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260928-trump-heads-to-gop-strongholds-alabama-and-oklahoma-to-campaign-for-midterms" /><summary type="html">President Donald Trump vowed to campaign in 35 of the most competitive battleground races in the final sprint to November's midterm elections. Instead, he will begin October by stumping in Alabama and Oklahoma, two of the most Republican states in the nation. France 24's Fraser Jackson takes a closer look.</summary></entry><entry><title>Pope wraps up France trip with most overtly political message of trip</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1d11143a99109d041498d4f026f099db7f1344e2527bd93d4baf85adca63c81e</id><updated>2026-09-28T16:50:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T13:57:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260928-pope-wraps-up-france-trip-with-most-overtly-political-message-of-trip" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo XIV urged Europe on Monday to draw from its Christian roots and traditions of dialogue to blunt the “desire for domination” driving today's wars, as he wrapped up a visit to France by recalling the forces that contributed to the continent's peaceful integration and made his post overtly political message of his trip.</summary></entry><entry><title>Pope touches on war, migration in speech at Metz</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6faee2f54920ccf5dab4763fa1ce1b5c4e9f1c1c9a512e12cf3c9effbeb13e4f</id><updated>2026-09-28T16:50:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T13:56:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260928-pope-touches-on-war-migration-in-speech-at-metz" /><summary type="html">Pope ​Leo urged Europe to remember ​its Christian history in a speech delivered in Metz, the ​hometown ‌of Robert ⁠Schuman, a founding father of ‌the European Union, during his four-day ⁠visit to France. Speaking in French, he urged Europeans to recall ‌the founding values of the EU, including the rule of law and the equality of all people without distinction of race, ⁠colour, class or profession.</summary></entry><entry><title>Author Katie Kitamura on why her book 'Audition' is also 'made by the reader'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5ce3277e75e3090caf1f9f44edf3fb030db1fd2c51b7f45777b6344f48f33b19</id><updated>2026-09-28T16:50:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T13:41:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20260928-author-katie-kitamura-on-why-her-book-audition-is-also-made-by-the-reader" /><summary type="html">The author Katie Kitamura, whose latest book has been nominated for both a Pulitzer and Booker Prize, has spoken to FRANCE 24 about her aim for the book to have been written by herself, but also with the reader alongside her.  "Audition" tells the story of an acclaimed actress whose life is turned upside down when a charismatic young man tells her he is her son. Kitamura says we all play different parts in our lives, and she is fascinated by the way they all interact. She spoke to us in Perspective.</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>Scottish indie darlings The Snuts return to their roots on 'Joy in Short Moments'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:865b1eb25ebf98497f9392647c76062a2911324250159eb6453cc0150160a108</id><updated>2026-09-28T16:50:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T13:32:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20260928-scottish-indie-darlings-the-snuts-return-to-their-roots-on-joy-in-short-moments" /><summary type="html">In this edition of our arts24 music show, Jennifer Ben Brahim chats with Jack Cochrane and Callum Wilson from Scottish indie four-piece The Snuts. They burst onto the music scene as the first Scottish band in over a decade to top the UK album charts. After years on the road and living in Glasgow, the band decided to move back to their home region of West Lothian. The return to their roots inspired the creation of their fourth album "Joy in Short Moments", a bittersweet record about success, failure, parenthood and loss.</summary><category term="arts24" /></entry><entry><title>Poll shows French far-right leader Marine Le Pen widening lead ahead of 2027 presidential vote</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3dfd8caf27cc2dd8a5ba26038b05784d8cfc7b301bdd9f166ff67c40dc1859d8</id><updated>2026-09-28T16:50:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T12:28:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260928-poll-shows-french-far-right-leader-marine-le-pen-widening-lead-ahead-of-2027-presidential-vote" /><summary type="html">Marine Le Pen, France's far-right National Rally party candidate, widened her lead in the second round of the 2027 presidential elections against both centre-right Édouard Philippe and hard-left Jean-Luc Mélenchon, according to a new poll released Monday.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>French prosecutors seek two-year sentence for Rachida Dati in Renault graft case</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:05df11933ed1a6257ab0163e56f938e9d9b4c247b7dcf44ed6f26139815cbfea</id><updated>2026-09-28T16:50:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T12:02:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260928-french-prosecutors-seek-two-year-sentence-for-ex-minister-dati-in-graft-case" /><summary type="html">French prosecutors have sought a two-year prison sentence for former culture minister Rachida Dati, to be served at home with an electronic tag, in a corruption case involving charges of lobbying for Renault-Nissan when she was a European lawmaker. The high-profile case centres on a contract signed in 2009 between Dati, who previously served as justice minister, and fugitive businessman Carlos Ghosn, then head of Renault-Nissan.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>Great Black Hope: Pursuit of belonging 'becomes a kind of cancer that eats them from the inside out'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2c42c6434be88b0ff3d7a8ac5034e90f92ddfe2025071f3a5bbf50c2fb93d38c</id><updated>2026-09-28T16:50:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T11:37:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/great-black-hope-pursuit-of-belonging-becomes-a-kind-of-cancer-that-eats-them-from-the-inside-out" /><summary type="html">Eve Irvine is pleased to welcome award-winning author Rob Franklin, joining us to discuss Great Black Hope, his acclaimed debut novel exploring race, class, respectability and belonging. Franklin wanted to write about the worlds he had spent years observing since childhood: including how class and race shape even our most intimate relationships.  At its centre is David Smith, a young Black man from a Southern bourgeois family. His education, manners and connections give him access, but he is constantly aware of the possibility of being cast out. That tension led him to think about respectability politics and the psychological cost of constantly performing an acceptable version of oneself.</summary></entry><entry><title>Le Pen hails 'victory' as French far right secures record 14 seats in Senate</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9e3f6bc44306ad7fa494676beb4883f18fd9d63bc1195cb5807655a935238f9f</id><updated>2026-09-28T16:50:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T11:22:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260928-le-pen-hails-victory-as-french-far-right-secures-record-14-seats-in-senate" /><summary type="html">France's far-right National Rally (RN) party and its allies emerged from polls with a record 14 seats in the right-wing dominated Senate on Sunday, effectively quadrupling its number in the 348-seat chamber just months before a presidential election.</summary></entry><entry><title>Pope wraps up 'hugely successful' France visit with Metz speech</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:85d88a65a8a5ac6125b6846299f76856949f177d63a2d1958a087cbe0c546ce4</id><updated>2026-09-28T16:50:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T11:20:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260928-pope-wraps-up-hugely-successful-france-visit-with-metz-speech" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo on Monday warned that relations between nations were becoming "increasingly uncivilised" with people boasting of "lies and deceit", and urged Europe to help "break this cycle"as he wrapped up what France 24's Angela Diffley says has been a "hugely successful" visit to France with a speech in Metz.</summary></entry><entry><title>Thailand floods: At least 8 die, thousands move to shelters</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:749752c3e3e1d6af1c71b69b85b0b6e935915c538233cb46458f660b48f1b879</id><updated>2026-09-28T16:50:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T11:20:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260928-thailand-floods-at-least-8-die-thousands-move-to-shelters" /><summary type="html">Rain eased in Thailand ’s capital on Sunday, but flooding persisted in several low-lying areas, with thousands forced to move into temporary shelters. At least eight people were reported killed in the past 10 days nationwide.</summary></entry><entry><title>REPLAY: Pope urges peace and unity in Europe on final day of France visit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:596481c49f978bf17a41f0c68f0775b69bf4bd12f1f80d60cb563298c4b52f80</id><updated>2026-09-28T16:50:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T10:49:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260928-replay-pope-urges-peace-and-unity-in-europe-on-final-day-of-france-visit" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo XIV urged Europe to remember its Christian history and appealed for peace and unity in a speech delivered in France's northeastern city of Metz on Monday, the fourth and final day of his visit.  "Relations between individuals and states are becoming increasingly uncivilised. The value of keeping one's word is dismissed. Instead, people boast of lies and deceit," he said. "Europe can help to break this cycle through the respect for others that it has learned to cultivate and preserve."</summary></entry><entry><title>Serbia's populist President Vucic resigns to run for PM</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cf30cb80ef5c7e11f256f79c30acd82861b136cc250722f5b50a0f8afbd8beb2</id><updated>2026-09-28T16:50:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T10:47:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260928-serbia-s-populist-president-vucic-resigns-to-run-for-pm" /><summary type="html">Serbia’s populist President Aleksandar Vucic resigned Sunday to pursue a bid to become prime minister in an upcoming early parliamentary election that will test his firm rule in the Balkan country, which was rattled by nearly two years of protests.</summary></entry><entry><title>REPLAY: France's Macron speaks on European Union as pope visits Metz</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6dfbf4d47bd72a237ed42124f0532c19c8b16ba3528f9da00148f51e333f3dae</id><updated>2026-09-28T16:50:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T10:42:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260928-replay-france-s-macron-speaks-on-european-union-as-pope-visits-metz" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron said that Europe must rediscover the “courage of its founders” and not give in to the “resurgence of nationalism" as he delivered an address alongside Pope Leo XIV in Metz on the last day of the pontiff's visit to France.</summary></entry></feed>
